            {
              "type": "reasoning.summary",
              "summary": "**Reflecting on wandering**\n\nAs I cross a signal, my mind effortlessly shifts its focus, possibly noticing connections I'd missed before\u2014like recalling a name that slipped my mind. It's subtle, yet the world feels slightly different. That's why I enjoy wandering without a goal; each route chosen for practicality transforms into an invitation to explore. I pass by familiar sights\u2014like a bakery or a colorful door\u2014without truly seeing them. This idle time allows the mind to relax, reminding me that being present is just as valuable as reaching a destination.**Carrying morning\u2019s essence**\n\nIn the evening, the city gathers its familiar noise once more. Yet, I still hold onto a bit of that morning's spaciousness, as if sunlight is lingering within me. It's a gentle reminder of the calm I experienced earlier in the day, even amidst the hustle and bustle. This blending of times makes me appreciate the contrast, allowing me to carry that peaceful feeling with me as I navigate the lively city.",
              "format": "openai-responses-v1",
              "index": 3
            },
